## Changes to the Standard Terms

1. **Acceptance (Section 10.16 and the definition of Cover Page).** Acceptance as described
   on this page is electronic acceptance of this Cover Page by Customer. Provider accepts by
   publishing it.
2. **Public terms (Section 9 and the definition of Confidential Information).** The existence
   and content of this page are public and are not Confidential Information.
3. **New versions (Section 10.2).** Provider may publish new versions of these Community
   Terms. Each version stays at its own permanent URL. Each release of the Software names the
   version that governs it, and Customer accepts that version by running the release with
   acceptance given.
4. **Updates (Section 1.6).** Provider may make Updates available but is not required to.
   Customer is not required to install them.
5. **Copies (Section 2.1).** Customer may make the copies reasonably needed to install, run,
   back up and internally mirror the Software for its Permitted Uses.
6. **Agents and contractors (Section 2.1).** Use of the Software by Customer's Users,
   contractors and AI agents, acting for Customer, is Customer's use. Customer is responsible
   for it.
7. **Customer's own customers (Sections 1.1 and 2.1).** Building and operating infrastructure
   and services that Customer provides to its own customers is use by Customer. It is not
   allowing others to access or use the Product, as long as those customers do not operate
   the Software themselves.
8. **Acceptance check (Section 2.1).** The acceptance check is a mechanism that controls the
   Software's functionality. Customer will not bypass or disable it except by accepting.
9. **Reviews and benchmarks (Section 2.1).** Section 2.1(a)(vi) does not apply. Customer may
   publish reviews, comparisons and benchmark results for the Software.
10. **Open source (Section 1.5).** The `turf` program's source code is published at
    https://github.com/turfbuild/turf under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, and that license
    governs the source code and anything Customer builds from it. Third-party components and
    their licenses are listed in the NOTICE file distributed with the Software.
11. **Ending this Agreement (Section 4).** Customer may end this Agreement at any time by
    following the Deletion Procedure. It ends automatically, with no cure period, if Customer
    breaches Section 1.1 or 2.1, or uses the Software outside the Permitted Uses after the
    grace period.
12. **Payment (Section 3).** Section 3 does not apply.
13. **Logo rights (Section 10.8).** Section 10.8 does not apply.
14. **Machine learning (Section 1.4).** Section 1.4 does not apply.
15. **Consumers.** Nothing in this Agreement limits rights Customer has as a consumer that
    cannot be waived under Applicable Laws.

